  "id": "COMPOUND:11293 - PROTEIN:6233",
  "verbalization": "Fenpiprane appears to have a shared target of the Bloom syndrome protein through multiple indirect pathways. The drug is linked to Sentrin-specific protease 7, which in turn is targeted by 5-Hydroxy-2-pyrrolidone and Jacaglabroside B, both of which ultimately target the Bloom syndrome protein. Similarly, Fenpiprane is also linked to Multidrug resistance-associated protein 7, which is targeted by Ugonin S, which also targets the Bloom syndrome protein. These findings suggest that Fenpiprane may exert its effects through a series of molecular interactions that ultimately converge on the Bloom syndrome protein. The evidence supports a mechanism where Fenpiprane influences cellular processes via proteolytic enzymes, potentially modulating pathways that are associated with the Bloom syndrome protein. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible role for Fenpiprane in regulating proteolytic activity, which could have implications for the broader biological functions of the Bloom syndrome protein.",
